WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.007 --> 00:00:02.250
- [Zac] "Halloween (2018)" is
filled with little references

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.870
and callbacks to the original "Halloween"

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.830
and its many sequels.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.510
For example, take this
scene where a father

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.430
and son come across the
escaped mental patients.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:09.690
Not only do their white outfits,

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.149
seemingly floating
around this foggy night,

00:00:11.149 --> 00:00:13.650
resemble the escaped patients
from the original "Halloween,"

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.725
but listen to the song
playing on the radio.

00:00:15.725 --> 00:00:16.912
- You all right?

00:00:16.912 --> 00:00:19.172
♪ I wish I had you all alone ♪

00:00:19.172 --> 00:00:22.755
♪ Just the two of us ♪

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:23.588
(kid gasps)

00:00:23.588 --> 00:00:25.440
- This is the same song that
we heard Laurie Strode singing

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.880
as she walked away from the Myers house

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.863
on that fateful day 40 years ago.

00:00:30.172 --> 00:00:34.784
♪ I wish I had you all alone ♪

00:00:34.784 --> 00:00:37.770
♪ Just the two of us ♪

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.080
- [Zac] The amazing thing is
this isn't even a real song.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.730
When speaking at Beyondfest 2014,

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.190
actress Jamie Lee Curtis revealed
that she just made it up,

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.389
which means for "Halloween (2018),"

00:00:45.389 --> 00:00:47.878
they actually created the rest
of the song and recorded it,

00:00:47.878 --> 00:00:49.740
just to include this Easter egg.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.120
I've gone through the entire movie

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.980
and picked out all of its best secrets.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.990
Once again, I will be
joined by "Halloween" expert

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.580
and horror YouTuber Jimmy Champane

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.440
who will be adding even
more "Halloween" insight

00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:59.273
and knowledge.

00:00:59.273 --> 00:01:00.106
- Hey, everyone.

00:01:00.106 --> 00:01:00.939
Happy Halloween.

00:01:00.939 --> 00:01:02.633
I'm glad to be back.
- [Zac] To learn the meaning

00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:04.080
behind the new opening title sequence,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.820
all of the "Halloween"
franchise Easter eggs,

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.970
my dark theory about Laurie
Strode and so much more,

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.190
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.256
This video is sponsored by Audible.

00:01:13.256 --> 00:01:15.673
(rock music)

00:01:19.117 --> 00:01:21.150
"Halloween (2018)" is not a remake,

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:23.340
but this episode of
"Things You Missed" is.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.200
I first covered the movie
when it was still in theaters,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.510
but since then I've noticed
many more hidden details

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:28.491
that I'm excited to talk about.

00:01:28.491 --> 00:01:31.350
The "Halloween" franchise is
no stranger to second chances.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.780
This movie is the second attempt
at making a direct sequel

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.010
to the original "Halloween."

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.170
The first was "Halloween II" from 1981,

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.030
which took place the same
night as the original.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.070
This one acts as if that
movie never happened

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.560
and brings us into the world
of Haddonfield 40 years later.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.880
Perhaps that's why we see a cop

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.230
playing "Back To The Future" pinball

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.940
before getting the call
about Michael Myers,

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.860
because this movie, like
"Back To The Future,"

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.050
is all about rewriting
the original timeline.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.730
The "Halloween" timeline
is like a train map,

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.620
which I like to call
the Halloween Express.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.750
I've done other videos
exploring alternate routes,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.799
but this time we're just going
directly from "Halloween 1"

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:03.090
to the first stop on this
line, "Halloween (2018)."

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.920
In future videos, I will
continue down this route

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.110
to "Halloween Kills" and "Halloween Ends."

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:08.970
Despite going in a different
direction with the plot,

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.530
there are still
similarities and references

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.737
to all of the other movies.

00:02:11.737 --> 00:02:14.310
"Halloween (2018)" is the
new "Halloween II" after all.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.570
It's not a remake in the sense

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.220
that it has the same story and characters.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.720
It's more of a reimagining.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.430
What if Laurie and Michael did not meet

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.600
for another 40 years?

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.608
So, lots of aspects from
the original "Halloween II"

00:02:23.608 --> 00:02:26.700
and everything else from the
last four decades do show up

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.744
in a slightly different form.

00:02:27.744 --> 00:02:30.744
I'll explain further once we
get into the things you missed.

00:02:31.681 --> 00:02:34.431
(dramatic music)

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.700
The movie opens at the mental
hospital, Smith's Grove.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.160
One of the first images
is the pen of Dr. Sartain.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.170
This pen ends up being important later on.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.050
We focus on it again the next day

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:46.080
as he is getting ready
for the patient transfer.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.880
And it's the same pen that
reveals a hidden blade

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:48.713
on Halloween night,

00:02:48.713 --> 00:02:51.180
so he can attack the police
officer and free Michael Myers.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:52.013
Perhaps this is

00:02:52.013 --> 00:02:53.670
why there's a little
spinal cord ornament on it.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.860
He's not literally stabbing
Deputy Hawkins in the back,

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.300
but it is a back stab in the sense

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.680
that he betrayed his trust.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.120
We see more shots around the hospital

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.220
as Dr. Sartain checks in
with one of his patients.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.780
It's difficult to hear what's being said,

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.180
so let me turn up the volume.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.882
- [Dr. Sartain] Did you have
a restful sleep last night?

00:03:06.882 --> 00:03:08.715
- [Patient] Oh yeah, I did.

00:03:08.715 --> 00:03:10.173
- [Dr. Sartain] Any dreams?

00:03:10.173 --> 00:03:11.006
- [Patient] Nope.

00:03:11.006 --> 00:03:12.400
- [Dr. Sartain] Sometimes we
don't remember our dreams,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.233
you know?

00:03:13.233 --> 00:03:14.066
- He's telling the patient

00:03:14.066 --> 00:03:15.660
about how we don't always
remember our dreams,

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.280
especially those that aren't recent.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.960
If you saw my episode on "Halloween II,"

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.490
you know that movie is all about dreams

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.170
and what goes on in the subconscious mind,

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.400
The whole movie is like a nightmare

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.750
that Laurie can't wake up from.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.580
I think the doctor's
dialogue is there to tell us

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:27.517
that in this continuity,

00:03:27.517 --> 00:03:29.610
"Halloween II" could be
considered nothing more

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:30.570
than a weird dream.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:31.668
There's further confirmation later

00:03:31.668 --> 00:03:33.376
when the character Dave makes this mistake

00:03:33.376 --> 00:03:35.373
about Laurie Strode's family history.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.580
- Wasn't it her brother

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:41.430
who like cold-blooded
murdelated all those teenagers?

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:42.420
- No.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.791
That's just a bit that some people made up

00:03:43.791 --> 00:03:45.390
to make them feel better I think.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.220
- So, this is a little
meta-joke to the audience.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:49.166
Allyson is clarifying that
the "Halloween II" plot twist

00:03:49.166 --> 00:03:51.630
where Laurie and Michael
are siblings is not canon

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.463
to this new timeline.

00:03:52.463 --> 00:03:54.382
Sartain takes the reporters
up to see Michael Myers

00:03:54.382 --> 00:03:56.715
and ask Aaron, the male
reporter, to tie his shoelace,

00:03:56.715 --> 00:03:58.366
so as not too upset one
of the mental patients

00:03:58.366 --> 00:04:00.232
who has a fixation about untied laces.

00:04:00.232 --> 00:04:02.065
I see this as another
message from the filmmakers

00:04:02.065 --> 00:04:04.610
to the audience; don't expect
a stereotypical slasher

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.450
where the victims trip
over their shoelaces

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:07.494
in life or death situations.

00:04:07.494 --> 00:04:09.702
This is the era of
elevated horror after all.

00:04:09.702 --> 00:04:11.160
It's less about outdated tropes

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.868
and more about disturbing subtext.

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:13.980
Whether they delivered

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.050
on this tied shoes promise is debatable.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.772
While it is true that nobody
trips on their shoelaces

00:04:17.772 --> 00:04:19.105
in "Halloween (2018),"

00:04:19.105 --> 00:04:21.390
there is a character who
gets killed after slipping

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.830
and falling on a hardwood floor.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.067
But the moment is a useful setup

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:25.650
because the character with
the shoelace fixation,

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.907
Mr. Tivoli, plays a
bigger part in the sequel,

00:04:27.907 --> 00:04:28.740
"Halloween Kills."

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.930
Aaron brings out the
original Michael Myers mask

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.220
to try to elicit a response,

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:34.175
but everyone besides Michael
seems to get riled up,

00:04:34.175 --> 00:04:36.258
which leads us to the opening credits.

00:04:36.258 --> 00:04:38.340
The classic "Halloween" title font is back

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.620
after being absent from
everything after "Halloween 4."

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.200
The opening credits introduce
Andi Matichack as Allyson,

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.730
Laurie Strode's teenage granddaughter.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:45.630
It's her first role,

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.171
just as the world was
introduced to Jamie Lee Curtis

00:04:47.171 --> 00:04:48.900
for the first time with "Halloween."

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:49.962
This is the first of many examples

00:04:49.962 --> 00:04:52.830
of Allyson filling the shoes
of Laurie Strode in this movie.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.878
You'll also notice the jack
o'lantern rotting in reverse.

00:04:54.878 --> 00:04:57.300
This may sound like the name
of a post-hardcore band,

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.932
but the image represents
Michael Myers rising

00:04:58.932 --> 00:05:01.080
back up to prominence after 40 years.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.862
In fact, the design of the
jack o'lantern is very similar

00:05:02.862 --> 00:05:04.070
to that of the original movie,

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.403
which many have suggested
looks like Michael in profile

00:05:06.403 --> 00:05:07.361
holding up a knife.

00:05:07.361 --> 00:05:09.090
After having no luck with Michael,

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:10.860
our Bri'ish repor'ers try to get Laurie

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:12.485
and her reaction to his impending transfer

00:05:12.485 --> 00:05:13.443
to a new facility.

00:05:13.443 --> 00:05:15.776
- You know he'll be locked
away until the end of his days.

00:05:15.776 --> 00:05:17.310
- That's the idea.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.680
- This is word for word what
Loomis said about his plan

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.110
to sedate Michael, so he can
barely sit up during his trial

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:22.943
in the first film.

00:05:22.943 --> 00:05:24.566
- He'll barely be able to sit up.

00:05:24.566 --> 00:05:26.970
- That's the idea.
- [Zac] I know Laurie thinks

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.560
that Dr. Sartain is the new Loomis,

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.240
so much so that she outright says so

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.760
as if she were an audience
member watching this movie.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.320
- You're the new Loomis.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.420
- But in many ways,
Laurie is the new Loomis.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.410
Be it her stark belief

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:38.910
that Michael is nothing more than evil,

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.063
her obsession with destroying him,

00:05:40.063 --> 00:05:42.450
her willingness to pull up and
scream at trick-or-treaters

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.295
who just end up seeing
her as a senile old lady,

00:05:44.295 --> 00:05:46.378
or her resourcefulness to
shoot and blow up Michael,

00:05:46.378 --> 00:05:48.211
there are certainly a lot of parallels.

00:05:48.211 --> 00:05:50.460
We're introduced to her
family shortly after.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.648
Her son-in-law, Ray, is setting
a mouse trap under the sink.

00:05:52.648 --> 00:05:54.298
I think this is a
foreshadowing of the ending

00:05:54.298 --> 00:05:56.880
where it's revealed that
Laurie's house is one big trap

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:57.865
for Michael Myers.

00:05:57.865 --> 00:05:59.820
- It's not a cage, baby.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:00.750
It's a trap.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.250
- [Zac] Pretty sure it's
still a cage though.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.810
When Allyson and her
friends walk to school,

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.940
the whole scene is an homage
to a scene from the original

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.753
where Laurie walks home with
her two high school friends.

00:06:07.753 --> 00:06:10.380
At one point, Dave stops
and blows up a pumpkin

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:11.419
with a firecracker.

00:06:11.419 --> 00:06:12.502
- Go, go, go, go, go!

00:06:12.502 --> 00:06:13.719
Happy Halloween!

00:06:13.719 --> 00:06:14.552
(pumpkin explodes)

00:06:14.552 --> 00:06:16.200
- This moment foreshadows
the end of the movie

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.520
where Laurie drops the same line

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.410
before releasing the
flare into the basement

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.660
to blow up her masked adversary.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.530
- Happy Halloween, Michael.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.280
(dramatic music)

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:32.340
- [Zac] "Halloween" is back this year

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:33.660
with a brand new installment.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.190
And if you've been with
the "Halloween" franchise

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:37.110
for a while, you might
remember the novelizations

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:39.180
that came out alongside
Halloweens one through four.

