00:07:33.532 --> 00:07:36.282
(dramatic music)

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.360
After Allyson tells about
her grandmother's history

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.863
with Michael Myers, her
friend Vicky suggests

00:07:40.863 --> 00:07:42.821
just ignoring the holiday altogether.

00:07:42.821 --> 00:07:44.700
- If I were you guys, I
wouldn't celebrate either.

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.220
I would just put up a
Christmas tree instead.

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:49.920
Just skip all over the
creepy Halloween shit, right?

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:50.753
- Uh, no.

00:07:50.753 --> 00:07:51.690
That's a terrible idea.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:53.283
But it might explain why
Laurie's daughter, Karen,

00:07:53.283 --> 00:07:55.094
wears a Christmas sweater
for the rest of the movie.

00:07:55.094 --> 00:07:57.210
I know I don't have to tell
this to "Halloween" fans,

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.510
but in my last video I
got a lot of questions

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:00.720
about what happened to
Laurie's daughter, Jamie.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:01.676
This all goes back to the timeline.

00:08:01.676 --> 00:08:04.134
Because "Halloween 4" never
happened in this continuity,

00:08:04.134 --> 00:08:05.430
Jamie was never born,

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.320
and Laurie has a daughter
named Karen instead.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.008
The scene inside Allyson's
class is another homage

00:08:09.008 --> 00:08:10.740
to a classic "Halloween" scene.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.450
You can pretty much count
on almost every scene

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:13.650
from here on out to be motivated

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:14.940
by sickening amounts of nostalgia.

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:16.800
Allyson sits in the back left seat,

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.731
the same position that
Laurie sat in in 1978.

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:20.939
The lesson is about fate,
just as Laurie's was.

00:08:20.939 --> 00:08:23.083
Guess they haven't updated
the curriculum lately.

00:08:23.083 --> 00:08:25.611
They also did this exact
same thing in "H2O" already.

00:08:25.611 --> 00:08:28.260
The twist in "H2O" is that
Laurie is now the teacher.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:31.320
This time, the teacher is played
by another familiar voice.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.400
- [Teacher] Now let's open our books

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.680
to Frankel's interpretation.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:37.950
He said, "Fate took a different course."

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.360
- Allyson's teacher is not seen,

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.550
but it's actually a vocal
cameo from PJ Soles,

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:43.680
the actress who played Lynda
in the first "Halloween."

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:45.360
Just as her grandmother
did years before her,

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:46.560
Allyson looks out the window.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:47.970
But where Laurie saw Michael Myers

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.020
standing there ominously,

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:51.150
Allyson sees Laurie
waiting to meet with her.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:52.950
This is part of the main
tenet of this movie,

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.480
the idea that the rolls of the hunter

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.880
and the hunted could be
reversed through perseverance.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.290
And this is what the
British reporters came

00:08:58.290 --> 00:08:59.670
to Haddonfield to investigate.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:01.687
In his recording, Aaron
poses the question,

00:09:01.687 --> 00:09:04.200
"Could it be that one
monster has created another?"

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.540
Later into Halloween night,
Dr. Sartain shares his theory

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.924
that both Laurie and Michael are vying

00:09:07.924 --> 00:09:09.273
to become the predator.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:14.370
- Michael's pursuit of
Laurie Strode could be

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:15.693
what keeps him alive.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.730
I would suspect the
notion of being a predator

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:24.690
or the fear of becoming prey
keeps both of them alive.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:26.550
- [Zac] Now we're seeing Laurie
has taken Michael's place

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:27.960
as the person standing outside the school,

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.378
and the movie contains many other examples

00:09:29.378 --> 00:09:32.550
of the roles being reversed,
mostly during the finale.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:33.919
In 1978, Laurie hides in the closet

00:09:33.919 --> 00:09:35.877
while Michael stalks the
house searching for her.

00:09:35.877 --> 00:09:38.210
But in 2018, Michael is
hidden somewhere in the house,

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.543
and Laurie is the one
investigating a shuttered closet.

00:09:40.543 --> 00:09:42.630
In '78, Michael's thrown off the balcony

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.873
after being shot by Dr. Loomis.
He's left lying in the yard,

00:09:44.873 --> 00:09:46.441
but on closer inspection, he vanishes.

00:09:46.441 --> 00:09:48.630
But in 2018, the rolls are reversed,

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.700
and Laurie is tossed from
the balcony in a scuffle.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:52.431
Michael sees her lying on the
ground in a familiar position,

00:09:52.431 --> 00:09:55.440
but after looking away
momentarily, she has disappeared.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.344
In '78, Michael's face
appears in a dark door frame

00:09:57.344 --> 00:09:59.610
to scare Laurie, the
coolest shot in the movie.

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.559
But in 2018, after Karen
shoots The Boogeyman,

00:10:01.559 --> 00:10:03.810
it is Laurie whose face
emerges from the dark

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:04.945
to strike fear into Michael.

00:10:04.945 --> 00:10:07.080
In her spare time, Laurie is
shown to practice shooting,

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.850
and essentially turns her
house into a fortress.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:10.530
She uses mannequins for target practice,

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:12.360
and after completely blowing
the head off this one,

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:13.800
uses the boobs as bullseyes.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.056
There's also a little kid mannequin.

00:10:15.056 --> 00:10:16.470
Very cool, Laurie.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:17.310
Very cool.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:18.570
There's a nice detail after this,

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:20.310
which is barely noticeable
in the final cut.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:22.140
Laurie has a big scar on her left shoulder

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.690
from where Michael cut her
sleeve open with a knife

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:24.690
in the original movie.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.528
There is a deleted scene where
we get a better look at it.

00:10:26.528 --> 00:10:28.861
She was not the only one to
take on damage that night.

00:10:28.861 --> 00:10:30.429
When we see Michael at
the mental hospital,

00:10:30.429 --> 00:10:32.262
there's a small scar visible on his neck.

00:10:32.262 --> 00:10:33.845
This is the same spot where Laurie got him

00:10:33.845 --> 00:10:36.240
with the knitting needle
all those years ago.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.386
As long as I'm bringing up deleted scenes,

00:10:37.386 --> 00:10:39.840
even they have a couple Easter eggs.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:40.673
In one deleted scene,

00:10:40.673 --> 00:10:42.540
Aaron scares Dana with
the Michael Myers mask

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:43.373
while she's showering,

00:10:43.373 --> 00:10:45.240
because apparently in
some alternate version

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.710
of this movie they were a couple.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:48.240
In "Halloween: The
Curse of Michael Myers,"

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:49.941
there's also a scene where
Michael sneaks up on someone

00:10:49.941 --> 00:10:50.880
in the shower.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:51.802
Another deleted scene shows a dog

00:10:51.802 --> 00:10:53.790
who became a Michael Myers victim.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:54.930
It's a common "Halloween" trope

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:56.670
for one of the earlier
victims to be a dog.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.747
It happens in the original,
"Return of Michael Myers,"

00:10:58.747 --> 00:11:01.470
"Revenge of Michael Myers," and
Rob Zombie's "Halloween II."

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.390
Michael and several other
patients are being transferred

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:05.010
from Smith's Grove to another facility.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.390
The idea of the patient transfer comes

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.250
from "Halloween 4: The
Return of Michael Myers,"

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:09.600
where Michael is loaded into a van,

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.310
and the trip has a similar outcome.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:12.750
This time it's a blue school bus,

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.580
which is a reference to
"The Purge" season one,

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:15.930
a fellow Blumhouse production.

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.347
I guess this was just
the year of blue buses

00:11:17.347 --> 00:11:20.070
because they did the blue
Fortnite bus in YouTube Rewind,

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.750
and Mr. Beast did it too.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:24.513
- Fortnite and Marques Brownlee.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:27.848
- Is this what you wanted?

00:11:27.848 --> 00:11:28.681
(Laurie screams)

00:11:28.681 --> 00:11:29.880
- [Zac] This was the
first "Halloween" title

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:31.980
to be made by Blumhouse, so
they decided to cross promote

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.900
with one of their big
properties, "The Purge."

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:35.717
The most recent film at the
time was "The First Purge,"

00:11:35.717 --> 00:11:38.070
and it features a big
"Halloween (2018)" poster

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:39.090
in a character's room.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.190
Allyson's boyfriend, Cameron,
is played by Dylan Arnold.

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:42.600
He's also from "The Purge."

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.666
The two are planning their
Halloween costumes as a couple.

00:11:44.666 --> 00:11:47.070
- So, we're going as Bonnie and Clyde.

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:48.210
- You know how it ended, right?

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:51.360
Their story ended with the
bullets and the bleeding.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:53.456
- That's probably a foreshadowing
of the end of this movie.

00:11:53.456 --> 00:11:55.617
Sure enough, it does end
with bullets and bleeding.

00:11:55.617 --> 00:11:57.678
But they aren't just
going as Bonnie and Clyde.

00:11:57.678 --> 00:12:00.060
Cameron will be rocking a skirt as Bonnie,

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.340
and Allyson complete with
neck tie will be Clyde.

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.620
It's Bonnie and Clyde but
with the roles reversed,

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.780
a symbol of the role reversal
between Michael and Laurie

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:07.890
where Laurie becomes the hunter

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.330
and Michael becomes the hunted.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:10.320
To foreshadow this switch,

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.330
the filmmakers feature the
reversal of traditional male

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.100
and female roles all over Haddonfield.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:15.870
For example, remember
that kid and his father

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.100
who came across the bus crash?

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:18.570
They're on the way home
from a hunting trip,

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:19.807
a typically male dominated activity.

00:12:19.807 --> 00:12:21.960
And the kid is complaining
about how he's upset

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:23.190
that he had to miss his dance class,

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:24.660
a typically female activity.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:25.991
There are three main love
interests in the movie;

00:12:25.991 --> 00:12:27.540
Allyson's boyfriend, Cameron,

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:28.650
Vicky's boyfriend, Dave,

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:29.483
and Karen's husband, Ray.

00:12:29.483 --> 00:12:31.590
They're all kind of sissy boys.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:33.180
Cameron throws his
girlfriend's phone in pudding

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:34.440
because he can't have her attention.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.820
Dave lets his girlfriend go upstairs

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:37.710
to investigate a strange
noise instead of him,

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:39.420
and it leads to her getting killed.

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:41.453
- Would you go look?
- [Dave] Do I have to?

00:12:41.453 --> 00:12:43.470
- [Zac] And Ray lets his
mother-in-law take the lead

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:45.090
while he does nothing
to protect the family.

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:47.130
None of these so-called
men take any initiative

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.000
in their relationship.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.950
Dave even puts a special
emphasis on the date

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.870
when he and his girlfriend
are gonna lose their virginity

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.460
and gets a tattoo of it on his shoulder.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.410
I don't know why, but to me
that just sounds like something

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:57.390
that a 15 year old girl
would find romantic.

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:59.490
Now nobody's saying that
being a girly boy is a good

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:00.323
or bad thing.

00:13:00.323 --> 00:13:01.156
My only point is

00:13:01.156 --> 00:13:02.910
that traditional gender
stereotypes have existed

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:05.880
for millions of years and
these characters ain't it.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:06.990
- I'll pop your cherry.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:08.401
- I do not wanna know what that entails.

00:13:08.401 --> 00:13:10.560
Also, Allyson's Clyde costume plays

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:11.880
into her becoming the new Laurie.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:14.040
She starts suited up with
a blazer, hat, and tie,

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.000
but as the night goes on,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.340
she loses any accessories that
might be slowing her down.

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:18.210
And in the final shot,

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:19.710
she's left with a blue button up shirt

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:21.060
with the top two buttons undone,

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:22.293
which leaves her looking
a lot like Laurie did

00:13:22.293 --> 00:13:24.501
when she was Allyson's age in 1978.

00:13:24.501 --> 00:13:26.959
During a dinner to celebrate
Allyson's academic achievement,

00:13:26.959 --> 00:13:29.042
there's this kind of bizarre
picture of a white horse

00:13:29.042 --> 00:13:30.180
in the restaurant.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:31.770
The white horse was part of a big metaphor

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.028
in Rob Zombie's "Halloween II."

00:13:33.028 --> 00:13:34.740
This is either a reference to that

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.310
or just they wanted a picture
of a horse in the restaurant.

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:39.471
Laurie is also depicted in the scene

00:13:39.471 --> 00:13:41.130
to have kind of a drinking problem,

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:42.000
just like her character

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.447
during the restaurant scene in "H20."

00:13:43.447 --> 00:13:45.180
Allyson's dad also talks about

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:47.250
how he used to know Cameron's
father, Lonnie Elam.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:48.660
Lonnie is actually a minor character

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:49.650
in the original "Halloween."

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:51.270
He's one of the kids
who teases Tommy Doyle

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:52.170
about The Boogeyman.

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:53.982
We see more of him later
in "Halloween Kills."

00:13:53.982 --> 00:13:55.950
It is not long after her arrival

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:57.450
that Laurie goes into freak out mode,

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:58.650
which leads into a flashback

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.570
where we see what it was
like for Karen growing up.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:03.384
And the house contains
a ton of hidden secrets.

00:14:03.384 --> 00:14:06.134
(thunder cracks)

00:14:08.423 --> 00:14:11.423
(suspenseful music)

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:13.740
Laurie shows up late to the dinner,

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:15.330
and she's acting a little strange.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.770
She's emotional after seeing Michael

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:18.060
during the hospital transfer.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:20.010
- I saw him.

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:20.970
The Shape.

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:22.320
- She calls him "The Shape."

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:23.370
If you're a "Halloween" fan,

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.200
you know that The Shape is
Michael's character name

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.810
in the end credits of
"Halloween" one, two, and six.

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:29.607
I believe this is the first
time a character refers to him

00:14:29.607 --> 00:14:31.350
as The Shape in universe though.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:32.520
I kind of like that they acknowledge

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:33.810
that somebody actually calls him that

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.160
without spoiling the mystique.

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:36.540
It's still up to the viewer to decide

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:37.854
what "The Shape" really means.

00:14:37.854 --> 00:14:38.812
They have to send Laurie home,

00:14:38.812 --> 00:14:40.530
and Karen finally tells her daughter

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:41.730
what her childhood was like.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:43.860
There are a ton of cool
details in Karen's room.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:44.693
Next to the window,

00:14:44.693 --> 00:14:46.170
we can see a little bit
of this poster frame,

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:48.154
the James Ensor painting. You
can get a better look at it

00:14:48.154 --> 00:14:49.881
when we come back to this
room at the end of the movie

00:14:49.881 --> 00:14:52.140
where we can also see the
black globe on the desk

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:53.400
and the hat hanging on the wall.

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:55.470
All three of these are items
that Laurie had in her room

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:57.155
as a teenager and held
onto over the years.

00:14:57.155 --> 00:14:58.238
There's another scene later on

00:14:58.238 --> 00:14:59.821
where Laurie shines a
flashlight into the room,

00:14:59.821 --> 00:15:01.279
and we see a heart-shaped pillow,

00:15:01.279 --> 00:15:03.487
another relic from
Laurie's room 40 years ago.

00:15:03.487 --> 00:15:05.320
Before I move on, there
are a couple more points

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:06.403
that I wanna make about the kid

00:15:06.403 --> 00:15:08.361
who discovered the crashed
patient transport bus.

00:15:08.361 --> 00:15:10.350
I'm really getting my
mileage out of this kid.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:11.670
He's in the movie for like two minutes,

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:13.398
and I already pulled three
things you missed off of him.

00:15:13.398 --> 00:15:15.822
After getting out to look for
his dad, he re-enters the car

00:15:15.822 --> 00:15:17.633
where Michael Myers is
now waiting for him.

00:15:17.633 --> 00:15:18.920
Michael chokes him from behind.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:21.450
This is the exact same way
that Annie Brackett died

00:15:21.450 --> 00:15:23.270
in her car in "Halloween (1978)."

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.230
As Michael slams the
kid against the window,

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:26.790
we get a rare glimpse at his face,

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.010
and you can see his left eye
has that clouded over look

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.447
that you sometimes see
with a blind person.

00:15:30.447 --> 00:15:32.880
This is the eye that Laurie
poked out with the coat hanger

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:33.713
at the end of the original.

00:15:33.713 --> 00:15:34.996
It's a little hard to see in this movie,

00:15:34.996 --> 00:15:36.990
so here's a behind the scenes photo.

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.430
One of the things I've
been keeping track of

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:40.010
in each of my "Halloween"
"Things You Missed" episodes

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:42.900
is the location of Haddonfield
within the state of Illinois.

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:44.610
The original took place
around the southern tip

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.207
near Hardin County, but both sequels,

00:15:46.207 --> 00:15:48.300
"Halloween 2" and "Halloween (2018),"

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.337
place Haddonfield in Warren
County off to the west.

00:15:50.337 --> 00:15:52.920
The next day is October 31st, Halloween.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.480
It's the best day of the year.

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:55.680
Our British reporters have decided

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.330
to visit the grave site of Judith Myers,

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:59.207
whose headstone has been
restored to its rightful place.

00:15:59.207 --> 00:16:01.950
I noticed this one big
recognizable gravestone

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:03.060
that says Sinclair,

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.440
because I remembered looking into this

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:05.730
when I analyzed "Halloween 1"

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:06.808
to see if it was anyone important.

00:16:06.808 --> 00:16:09.304
It wasn't, but the fact that
this is here in 2018 means

00:16:09.304 --> 00:16:11.760
that they either went back
to the exact same spot

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:14.231
or created a graveyard set
with great attention to detail.

00:16:14.231 --> 00:16:16.041
Either way, job well done by someone.

00:16:16.041 --> 00:16:17.379
If anyone is an expert on trees,

00:16:17.379 --> 00:16:18.337
let me know if it's possible

00:16:18.337 --> 00:16:20.190
that this skinny tree could have grown

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:21.367
into this massive chonker of a tree

00:16:21.367 --> 00:16:23.163
in the 40 years between these movies.

00:16:23.163 --> 00:16:24.870
Sorry for calling it that.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.270
I got a little carried away.

00:16:27.454 --> 00:16:28.650
(computer beep)

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.870
Another similarity between the
films is the groundskeepers.

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:32.910
In the first one, the
guy tells Loomis a story

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:34.380
from the nearby town Russellville.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.180
In this one, the groundskeeper
talks about her cousin

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.041
who works in another
cemetery in a nearby town.

00:16:38.041 --> 00:16:40.712
That morning, Deputy Hawkins
discovers Michael Myers is one

00:16:40.712 --> 00:16:41.925
of the escaped mental patients.

00:16:41.925 --> 00:16:43.103
On the document he's holding,

00:16:43.103 --> 00:16:45.540
the patient is listed as Michael A. Myers.

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.400
The middle initial A stands for Audrey,

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.620
which is a reference that
not many viewers know about.

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:51.720
The original "Halloween"
was filmed in 1978

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:52.980
and released that same year.

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:54.630
It became very popular, so in 1980,

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:57.248
NBC bought the rights to
air the film on television.

00:16:57.248 --> 00:16:58.830
It was only 91 minutes,

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.380
so NBC asked John Carpenter to
film a few additional scenes

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:02.640
to fit a two hour time slot

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:03.930
so they could show more commercials.

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:06.212
That's where they reveal
Michael's middle name, Audrey.

00:17:06.212 --> 00:17:09.670
- I have no choice but to
remand Michael Audrey Myers

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:13.350
to the Smith's Grove
Warren County Sanitarium.

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:15.240
- Next we've got another
set that pays homage

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:16.387
to scenes of "Halloween" past.

00:17:16.387 --> 00:17:18.690
The gas station that
Aaron and Dana fill up at

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:21.060
brings to mind the gas station
that Dr. Loomis stops at

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:21.893
in "Halloween 4."

00:17:21.893 --> 00:17:23.520
This is where Michael attacks a mechanic

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:24.953
to steal his jumpsuit in both movies.

00:17:24.953 --> 00:17:25.786
If you look closely,

00:17:25.786 --> 00:17:28.080
Michael is actually the
driver of the brown truck

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:29.970
that pulls up on the far
end of the parking lot.

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:32.460
Michael also hijacked a
brown car in "Halloween."

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:34.020
We can actually see him crossing over

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:36.330
to go into the service shop
while Aaron has his back turned,

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.340
then again when Dana steps into the store.

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:39.360
If you look through this window,

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:41.010
Michael can be seen attacking the mechanic

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:41.880
in the background.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:43.380
Next to where Aaron is refueling,

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:45.279
a red van pulls up from
Resurrection Church,

00:17:45.279 --> 00:17:47.040
and there's a strange woman inside.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:48.453
This may be one of our only references

00:17:48.453 --> 00:17:49.927
to the eighth "Halloween" film,

00:17:49.927 --> 00:17:52.210
"Halloween Resurrection" from 2002.

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.700
(static rumbles)

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:54.690
I also want to note that

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:56.280
when Michael Myers stranded Dr. Loomis

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:57.780
at the gas station in "Halloween 4,"

00:17:57.780 --> 00:17:59.820
it was a strange Reverend
whose car was decorated

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:01.560
with religious stickers who picked him up.

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:02.610
Before meeting the Reverend,

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.050
he tried to hitchhike
with some cheerleaders

00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:05.790
in a convertible, but
they left him in the dust

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:06.623
when he got close.

00:18:06.623 --> 00:18:08.392
There is a deleted scene
from "Halloween (2018)"

00:18:08.392 --> 00:18:10.230
that seems to reference this moment,

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.864
but it's definitely
referencing another moment.

00:18:11.864 --> 00:18:13.830
Listen to what the
cheerleaders are chanting.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:17.160
- We're from Haddonfield,
couldn't be prouder!

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:17.993
Can't hear us now?

00:18:17.993 --> 00:18:19.860
We'll yell a little louder!

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.540
- I guess some traditions never die

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:23.610
because this one goes back
to the first "Halloween."

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:26.160
- We're from Haddonfield,
couldn't be prouder!

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:26.993
Can't hear us now?

00:18:26.993 --> 00:18:28.530
We'll yell a little louder!

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:30.424
- There are so many similarities
between these scenes.

00:18:30.424 --> 00:18:32.400
In both movies, characters start talking

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:33.450
about the Halloween dance

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:35.084
immediately after walking
away from the cheerleaders.

00:18:35.084 --> 00:18:37.080
The high school's sign has been updated,

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.324
but they're still short on black letters,

00:18:38.324 --> 00:18:39.960
so they use a few red ones.

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:40.860
Details like this are

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:43.110
why this movie is
considered a requel by fans.

00:18:43.110 --> 00:18:43.943
It's technically a sequel,

00:18:43.943 --> 00:18:46.042
but it feels like a remake
with how repetitive it is.

00:18:46.042 --> 00:18:48.604
At the time, I compared it to
"Star Wars: The Force Awakens"

00:18:48.604 --> 00:18:50.017
which basically does the same thing.

00:18:50.017 --> 00:18:51.997
It's a requel of the original "Star Wars."

00:18:51.997 --> 00:18:54.005
"Jurassic World" was a
requel of "Jurassic Park."

00:18:54.005 --> 00:18:55.838
All three of these were
insanely profitable,

00:18:55.838 --> 00:18:57.693
so now requels are everywhere.

00:18:57.693 --> 00:19:00.960
So, the homages, callbacks,
whatever you wanna call them,

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:02.130
they just keep coming.

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:03.990
Like, every 45 seconds or so.

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:04.856
Dana steps into the ladies room

00:19:04.856 --> 00:19:06.331
where she's attacked by Michael Myers.

00:19:06.331 --> 00:19:08.601
That's a reference to
"Halloween H2O: 20 Years Later,"

00:19:08.601 --> 00:19:10.230
where that same thing happens.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:11.280
Aaron comes in to save her

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:13.170
but he gets his face bashed
into the bathroom wall.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.000
That's a reference to the
"Halloween" remake directed

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:15.833
by Rob Zombie.

00:19:15.833 --> 00:19:16.920
I find it somewhat interesting

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.557
that Michael bashes in
the face of this reporter

00:19:18.557 --> 00:19:21.150
in order to regain his iconic face,

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:23.039
or at least William Shatner's iconic face.

00:19:23.039 --> 00:19:25.140
Yeah, I've never stopped
thinking about this guy

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:26.557
on my original videos who said,

00:19:26.557 --> 00:19:28.627
"Micheal does not have Shatner's face.

00:19:28.627 --> 00:19:30.630
"It's the other way around."

00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:31.860
What the hell are you on, man?

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:33.675
Suppose Shatner's mom
could somehow dictate

00:19:33.675 --> 00:19:35.147
how her baby's face came out.

00:19:35.147 --> 00:19:36.867
She would also need time travel.

00:19:36.867 --> 00:19:38.490
Shatner was born in the '30s,

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:40.337
almost 50 years before
"Halloween" came out.

00:19:40.337 --> 00:19:41.701
With Michael's costume complete,

00:19:41.701 --> 00:19:43.860
he's ready to do some trick-or-treating.

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:45.600
I hope you're not tired
of the constant callbacks

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:46.650
to previous "Halloween" movies

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:48.367
because this next part is
something I like to call

00:19:48.367 --> 00:19:49.628
"the 'Halloween II' sequence."

00:19:49.628 --> 00:19:52.573
Three minutes and 45 seconds
of pure nostalgia pron

00:19:52.573 --> 00:19:55.020
for Halloween's 1981 sequel.

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:56.550
It starts with these two kids.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.207
The one on the left is
dressed up as a pirate.

00:19:58.207 --> 00:19:59.979
"Halloween II" had a pirate
kid who went to the hospital

00:19:59.979 --> 00:20:02.310
after getting a razor
in his Halloween candy.

00:20:02.310 --> 00:20:03.970
The kid on the right is a
cowboy holding a boombox

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.880
on his shoulder, and
he bumps into Michael,

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:07.800
but Michael ignores him
and continues on his way.

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:09.570
This exact thing happens in "Halloween II"

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:11.340
before Michael makes
his way to the hospital.

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:13.590
Then Michael goes between
these houses to snoop around.

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.649
You can hear some kids
singing in the background.

00:20:15.649 --> 00:20:19.739
♪ Black cats and goblins
and broomsticks and ghosts ♪

00:20:19.739 --> 00:20:23.640
♪ Covens of witches with
all of their hosts ♪

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:25.680
- This is actually another
"Halloween 1" reference.

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:27.480
It's the same chant that we
hear at the very beginning,

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:28.860
right after the opening titles.

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.351
♪ Black cats and goblins
and broomsticks and ghosts ♪

00:20:32.351 --> 00:20:35.853
♪ Covens of witches with
all of their hosts ♪

00:20:35.853 --> 00:20:38.160
- [Zac] Then Michael goes into
the shed and gets a hammer.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:39.810
The first weapon he
acquires at the hospital

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:41.490
in "Halloween II" is a hammer.

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:43.680
I think the existence of the
"Halloween II" sequence goes

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:44.880
back to what I said earlier,

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.500
because this movie represents the start

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:47.366
of a new timeline branch,

00:20:47.366 --> 00:20:49.980
this is the new "Halloween 2" in a sense.

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:51.870
In H2, Michael broke
into the Elrod's house

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:53.094
where Mr. Elrod is watching TV.

00:20:53.094 --> 00:20:55.046
The TV is also on here in 2018,

00:20:55.046 --> 00:20:57.686
but the program is the
1982 series "Voyager."

00:20:57.686 --> 00:20:59.730
This show is about a
pair of time travelers

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.669
who go back to repair
errors in world history.

00:21:01.669 --> 00:21:03.861
In other words, they are
altering the timeline,

00:21:03.861 --> 00:21:06.115
just as David Gordon Green, Danny McBride,

00:21:06.115 --> 00:21:07.806
and Jeff Fradley are
rewriting the timeline

00:21:07.806 --> 00:21:10.089
of the "Halloween" franchise
by taking out plot points

00:21:10.089 --> 00:21:11.730
that they consider to be errors,

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:14.077
such as Laurie and Michael
being related by blood.

00:21:14.077 --> 00:21:16.140
"Halloween (2018)" in a way reminds me

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:18.240
of Steven King's "11/22/63."

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:19.980
You can go back and change certain events,

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:20.955
but there are still inevitables

00:21:20.955 --> 00:21:22.288
that are going to happen no matter what,

00:21:22.288 --> 00:21:24.330
which is why the "Halloween
II" sequence continues

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:27.471
with even more things you missed.

00:21:27.471 --> 00:21:30.221
(thunder cracks)

00:21:31.932 --> 00:21:34.682
(dramatic music)

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:37.410
Michael's next victim is Mrs. Elrod,

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:39.309
a woman in a pink bathrobe
with hair curlers,

00:21:39.309 --> 00:21:40.770
making a ham sandwich.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:42.480
She's an homage to Mrs. Elrod,

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:44.220
the woman that Michael
steals a kitchen knife from

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:45.429
in "Halloween II."

00:21:45.429 --> 00:21:48.262
- Mrs. Elrod?

00:21:48.262 --> 00:21:49.095
Mr. Elrod?

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:53.520
Are you okay?

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:55.680
- We don't see Mr. Elrod
in "Halloween (2018),"

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:57.210
but there is a reference to him later on

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:58.800
when Allyson's friend Oscar is drunk

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:00.360
in the Elrod's backyard.

00:22:00.360 --> 00:22:02.040
- Happy Halloween, Mr. Elrod.

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:03.990
- [Zac] 2018's Mrs. Elrod is not as lucky

00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:05.911
as her H2 counterpart,
and after finishing her,

00:22:05.911 --> 00:22:07.205
Michael continues through the house

00:22:07.205 --> 00:22:08.910
where we hear a crying baby.

00:22:08.910 --> 00:22:10.980
But Michael does not bother
going after the baby,

00:22:10.980 --> 00:22:13.475
which may be a nod to the
original and the 2007 remake

00:22:13.475 --> 00:22:16.200
where Michael ignores kids
and babies during his spree.

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:17.344
Outside, a couple dressed as a doctor

00:22:17.344 --> 00:22:19.530
and nurse are leaving their house.

00:22:19.530 --> 00:22:20.430
- Wait, hang on, hang on.

00:22:20.430 --> 00:22:21.746
I don't have my stethoscope.

00:22:21.746 --> 00:22:23.340
- [Zac] "Halloween II"
takes place at a hospital

00:22:23.340 --> 00:22:25.050
in Haddonfield, so you
can bet there are plenty

00:22:25.050 --> 00:22:26.850
of scandalous nurses there as well.

00:22:26.850 --> 00:22:28.650
This is also a setup for "Halloween Kills"

00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:31.020
where these characters would
come back in a bigger capacity.

00:22:31.020 --> 00:22:32.250
But instead of going after them,

00:22:32.250 --> 00:22:34.410
Michael turns to his right
and stares through the window

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:37.304
at this woman talking on the
phone to someone named Sally.

00:22:37.304 --> 00:22:38.760
- [Woman] Hey, Sally, how are you?

00:22:38.760 --> 00:22:40.695
- [Zac] Mrs. Elrod's neighbor
in "Halloween II" is also

00:22:40.695 --> 00:22:43.140
on the phone with a girl named Sally.

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:45.120
- Sally, I can hear the sirens coming.

00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:45.972
- Judging by the conversation,

00:22:45.972 --> 00:22:48.191
this woman is also learning
about the latest incident

00:22:48.191 --> 00:22:50.550
in Haddonfield during this phone call.

00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:51.510
- [Woman] Really?

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:52.365
That's awful.

00:22:52.365 --> 00:22:53.820
- And in both movies,

00:22:53.820 --> 00:22:56.298
Michael sneaks up with a little surprise.

00:22:56.298 --> 00:22:59.130
(woman screams)

00:22:59.130 --> 00:23:01.620
And that is the three
minutes and 45 seconds

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:04.740
that I collectively refer to
as the "Halloween II" sequence.

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:06.705
After that, it's straight back
to "Halloween 1" memories.

00:23:06.705 --> 00:23:08.218
No "Halloween" requel would be complete

00:23:08.218 --> 00:23:10.350
without at least one babysitter,

00:23:10.350 --> 00:23:12.000
since the only reason
that Laurie and Annie

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:13.144
ever encountered Michael Myers was

00:23:13.144 --> 00:23:15.030
because they were
babysitting across the street

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:15.863
from each other.

00:23:15.863 --> 00:23:17.991
This time, Vicky is
babysitting a kid named Julian,

00:23:17.991 --> 00:23:21.360
or as I like to call him, the
best character in the movie.

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:23.190
Her boyfriend is already
on the way to join her

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:24.270
for a spicy evening.

00:23:24.270 --> 00:23:26.594
And Allyson and Cameron are
supposed to stop by after that.

00:23:26.594 --> 00:23:28.802
She's setting up a very similar
scenario to what went on

00:23:28.802 --> 00:23:31.200
at the Wallace household in 1978,

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:32.306
where Annie invites her boyfriend,

00:23:32.306 --> 00:23:34.740
and Lynda and Bob used
the house to get busy.

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:36.152
However, like in "Halloween 1,"

00:23:36.152 --> 00:23:38.175
things don't go according to plan.

00:23:38.175 --> 00:23:40.740
While Allyson and Cameron are
attending the Halloween dance,

00:23:40.740 --> 00:23:41.595
presumably the same dance

00:23:41.595 --> 00:23:43.680
that Laurie hoped Ben
Tramer would take her to,

00:23:43.680 --> 00:23:45.660
Allyson sees Cameron kiss another girl,

00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:48.120
and she storms off causing
him to chase after her.

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:49.565
I'm not sure if this is
an intentional reference

00:23:49.565 --> 00:23:51.900
or anything, but it sure
is a lot like this scene

00:23:51.900 --> 00:23:54.180
from "Halloween 4" where
Rachel Carruthers gets upset

00:23:54.180 --> 00:23:55.430
after seeing the boy
that she's interested in

00:23:55.430 --> 00:23:56.670
with the Sheriff's daughter

00:23:56.670 --> 00:23:58.260
who's wearing this "cops
do it by the book" shirt

00:23:58.260 --> 00:24:00.360
and basically nothing else.

00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:01.740
As a result, they break up,

00:24:01.740 --> 00:24:02.650
so the after party is limited

00:24:02.650 --> 00:24:05.070
to just Vicky, Dave, and Julian.

00:24:05.070 --> 00:24:07.316
Oh, and one other guest.

00:24:07.316 --> 00:24:09.450
(suspenseful music)
(Vicky screams)

00:24:09.450 --> 00:24:10.283
Cops are called,

00:24:10.283 --> 00:24:11.415
and we hear the following
communication go out

00:24:11.415 --> 00:24:12.690
over police radios.

00:24:12.690 --> 00:24:14.456
- [Radio] All units, we have reports

00:24:14.456 --> 00:24:17.460
of a domestic disturbance
at 707 Meridian Avenue.

00:24:17.460 --> 00:24:19.860
- This is another little
Easter egg for movie fans.

00:24:19.860 --> 00:24:21.420
The original "Halloween" was filmed in

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:22.473
and around Pasadena, California,

00:24:22.473 --> 00:24:25.517
and 707 Meridian Avenue was
the address of the Myers house.

00:24:25.517 --> 00:24:28.217
You can still visit it and
many locations from the movie,

00:24:28.217 --> 00:24:30.300
like the corner store
and the Strode house.

00:24:30.300 --> 00:24:31.593
Speaking of the Myers house,

00:24:31.593 --> 00:24:33.780
when I made my initial
video in this movie,

00:24:33.780 --> 00:24:36.270
I assumed that the dollhouse
in Karen's room was a replica

00:24:36.270 --> 00:24:37.267
of the Myers house.

00:24:37.267 --> 00:24:38.688
"Halloween (2018)" was still
in theaters at the time,

00:24:38.688 --> 00:24:41.340
so I didn't really have the
opportunity to compare it.

00:24:41.340 --> 00:24:42.262
And it does look kind of similar,

00:24:42.262 --> 00:24:44.984
but upon closer inspection,
it's clearly not.

00:24:44.984 --> 00:24:46.890
The Myers house doesn't
have these dormers.

00:24:46.890 --> 00:24:48.540
It doesn't have a window
above the front door.

00:24:48.540 --> 00:24:49.813
And the inner layout is not similar at all

00:24:49.813 --> 00:24:51.529
to what we see from "Halloween"'s opening.

00:24:51.529 --> 00:24:53.250
It's not the Myers house,

00:24:53.250 --> 00:24:54.320
but that didn't stop certain websites

00:24:54.320 --> 00:24:57.300
that like to steal my writing
from saying that it is

00:24:57.300 --> 00:24:59.250
without actually checking for themselves.

00:24:59.250 --> 00:25:00.450
No surprises there.

00:25:00.450 --> 00:25:02.180
Interestingly, there's another
little light blue house

00:25:02.180 --> 00:25:03.030
in the background

00:25:03.030 --> 00:25:04.740
during the interview scene
in Laurie's living room.

00:25:04.740 --> 00:25:06.180
It is also not the Myers house,

00:25:06.180 --> 00:25:08.130
but it's not identical
to the dollhouse either.

00:25:08.130 --> 00:25:10.560
I think the dollhouse just
represents Karen's childhood.

00:25:10.560 --> 00:25:12.120
Karen always wanted to be a normal kid,

00:25:12.120 --> 00:25:13.920
but Laurie wanted to train her for combat.

00:25:13.920 --> 00:25:15.612
At the end of the movie,
the dollhouse is lit on fire

00:25:15.612 --> 00:25:17.973
after Karen uses her training
to help defeat Michael.

00:25:17.973 --> 00:25:20.431
The image represents Karen
trading a normal childhood

00:25:20.431 --> 00:25:22.389
for protection all of these years later.

00:25:22.389 --> 00:25:23.265
One "Halloween" film

00:25:23.265 --> 00:25:24.967
that doesn't often get referenced is

00:25:24.967 --> 00:25:26.700
"Halloween III: Season of the Witch"

00:25:26.700 --> 00:25:28.389
because it's the only one
that's completely disconnected

00:25:28.389 --> 00:25:30.120
from the rest of the franchise.

00:25:30.120 --> 00:25:30.953
The movie is about the mystery

00:25:30.953 --> 00:25:33.390
of an evil mask making company
known as Silver Shamrock.

00:25:33.390 --> 00:25:35.735
This scene in "Halloween
(2018)" shows trick-or-treaters

00:25:35.735 --> 00:25:37.693
wearing the three Silver Shamrock masks;

00:25:37.693 --> 00:25:39.637
skeleton, jack o'lantern, and witch.

00:25:39.637 --> 00:25:40.611
Deputy Hawkins shows up

00:25:40.611 --> 00:25:42.570
at the house Vicky has
been babysitting at,

00:25:42.570 --> 00:25:43.983
outside of which we see
a clothesline covered

00:25:43.983 --> 00:25:45.066
in hanging white sheets.

00:25:45.066 --> 00:25:46.524
You'd be hard pressed to find anyone

00:25:46.524 --> 00:25:49.107
who doesn't use a machine to
dry their clothes in 2018,

00:25:49.107 --> 00:25:51.570
so I see this as a slight
nod to the original

00:25:51.570 --> 00:25:52.523
where Michael Myers stalks Laurie

00:25:52.523 --> 00:25:53.940
from behind a clothesline.

00:25:53.940 --> 00:25:54.939
When I covered the original "Halloween"

00:25:54.939 --> 00:25:55.980
on "Things You Missed,"

00:25:55.980 --> 00:25:58.100
I talked about how this is part
of a psychosexual metaphor,

00:25:58.100 --> 00:26:00.240
but in just about every
episode since then,

00:26:00.240 --> 00:26:02.164
I've pointed out more
examples of hanging sheets.

00:26:02.164 --> 00:26:03.622
It's pretty much become
a "Halloween" tradition

00:26:03.622 --> 00:26:06.240
at this point to have them
show up somewhere in the movie.

00:26:06.240 --> 00:26:07.073
Another use of white sheets,

00:26:07.073 --> 00:26:08.996
both in the original
"Halloween" and this movie,

00:26:08.996 --> 00:26:10.950
is the bed sheet ghost costume.

00:26:10.950 --> 00:26:12.930
This time instead of
using it as a disguise,

00:26:12.930 --> 00:26:13.812
it's used as a red herring.

00:26:13.812 --> 00:26:15.284
Michael drapes it over Vicky's corpse

00:26:15.284 --> 00:26:17.160
for Deputy Hawkins to discover.

00:26:17.160 --> 00:26:19.084
Vicky is also set up in a
chair next to a fish tank.

00:26:19.084 --> 00:26:20.966
It's like when the nurse
discovers what Michael did

00:26:20.966 --> 00:26:22.719
to Dr. Mixter in "Halloween II."

00:26:22.719 --> 00:26:24.772
Next, Hawkins goes downstairs to find Dave

00:26:24.772 --> 00:26:26.520
who is pinned to the wall with a knife,

00:26:26.520 --> 00:26:28.860
the same fate that Bob Simms
suffered in "Halloween."

00:26:28.860 --> 00:26:31.080
If all of these repeated scenes
and homages weren't enough,

00:26:31.080 --> 00:26:32.740
there are also numerical references

00:26:32.740 --> 00:26:33.948
to other "Halloween" movies.

00:26:33.948 --> 00:26:37.235
The cop car that shows up for
reinforcement is number 1078.

00:26:37.235 --> 00:26:40.560
The babysitter murders took
place in October of 1978.

00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:42.417
Deputy Hawkins vehicle is 1098.

00:26:42.417 --> 00:26:43.320
So, that would be the month

00:26:43.320 --> 00:26:45.845
that "Halloween H2O" took
place; October, 1998.

00:26:45.845 --> 00:26:48.217
And yes, that means this
movie is technically

00:26:48.217 --> 00:26:50.490
"Halloween H40: 40 Years Later."

00:26:50.490 --> 00:26:52.080
Can't wait for H6O.

00:26:52.080 --> 00:26:54.420
Laurie shows up to warn Karen
and Ray that they aren't safe,

00:26:54.420 --> 00:26:56.250
and they leave a message for Allyson.

00:26:56.250 --> 00:26:58.890
- There is a police officer
waiting at your house

00:26:58.890 --> 00:26:59.910
to bring you to us.

00:26:59.910 --> 00:27:02.010
We're all gonna be together.

00:27:02.010 --> 00:27:04.020
Now do as I say.

00:27:04.020 --> 00:27:05.655
- She used these same words 40 years prior

00:27:05.655 --> 00:27:08.400
to protect Tommy Doyle
and Lindsey Wallace.

00:27:08.400 --> 00:27:10.650
- I want you to tell
them to call the police

00:27:10.650 --> 00:27:12.205
and tell 'em to send 'em over here.

00:27:12.205 --> 00:27:14.730
Now, do you understand me?

00:27:14.730 --> 00:27:15.870
Go, do as I say!

00:27:15.870 --> 00:27:17.250
- Part of the reason this "Halloween" was

00:27:17.250 --> 00:27:18.810
such a big event in the horror world was

00:27:18.810 --> 00:27:21.079
that horror movies were at near
peak popularity at the time.

00:27:21.079 --> 00:27:22.568
This was only a year after "It"

00:27:22.568 --> 00:27:25.298
and two years after "Lights
Out" and many other bangers.

00:27:25.298 --> 00:27:27.810
In fact, it seems the writers
of this new "Halloween" were

00:27:27.810 --> 00:27:30.150
very inspired by "Lights
Out" as the scene with Oscar

00:27:30.150 --> 00:27:31.710
and the motion censored
light features Michael

00:27:31.710 --> 00:27:32.826
at a standstill when the light is on,

00:27:32.826 --> 00:27:34.409
but he creeps up close to his target

00:27:34.409 --> 00:27:35.617
each time the light goes off.

00:27:35.617 --> 00:27:38.490
This is exactly how the
antagonist Diana gets you

00:27:38.490 --> 00:27:39.330
in "Lights Out."

00:27:39.330 --> 00:27:41.616
This wasn't the first or last
movie to borrow this concept.

00:27:41.616 --> 00:27:43.653
But whether this imitation
was a form of flattery

00:27:43.653 --> 00:27:46.527
or theft is ultimately
up to you to decide.

00:27:46.527 --> 00:27:47.760
But I think it's theft.

00:27:47.760 --> 00:27:49.469
I was amused to see that
"Halloween" takes another page

00:27:49.469 --> 00:27:51.120
from "Lights Out" later in the movie.

00:27:51.120 --> 00:27:52.800
The mannequin scene where
Laurie is looking around

00:27:52.800 --> 00:27:54.380
for Michael in the house
is very reminiscent

00:27:54.380 --> 00:27:55.213
of the factory scene

00:27:55.213 --> 00:27:56.910
at the beginning of the
feature film version

00:27:56.910 --> 00:27:57.780
of "Lights Out."

00:27:57.780 --> 00:27:59.910
After seeing Oscar get "The
Virgin Suicides" treatments

00:27:59.910 --> 00:28:02.430
on the Elrods' fence, Allyson
runs, screams for help,

00:28:02.430 --> 00:28:04.110
and begs a neighbor to let her inside,

00:28:04.110 --> 00:28:05.461
the same reaction that teenage Laurie had

00:28:05.461 --> 00:28:06.669
to seeing her dead friends.

00:28:06.669 --> 00:28:08.334
The difference is that
Allyson actually gets someone

00:28:08.334 --> 00:28:09.292
to let her inside.

00:28:09.292 --> 00:28:11.750
Maybe we can chalk this up to
the existence of technology

00:28:11.750 --> 00:28:13.708
in the '10s that would've
allowed the neighbors to know

00:28:13.708 --> 00:28:14.791
that Michael was on the loose

00:28:14.791 --> 00:28:17.081
and Allyson probably wasn't pranking them.

00:28:17.081 --> 00:28:19.244
The final act of this movie
would contain more info

00:28:19.244 --> 00:28:21.660
about the true intentions of Dr. Sartain,

00:28:21.660 --> 00:28:23.820
and I have my own theory
about a dark secret

00:28:23.820 --> 00:28:26.561
from none other than Laurie Strode.

00:28:26.561 --> 00:28:29.311
(thunder cracks)

00:28:35.430 --> 00:28:36.317
After picking up Allyson,

00:28:36.317 --> 00:28:38.910
Deputy Hawkins heads towards
Laurie's fortress of a house

00:28:38.910 --> 00:28:41.068
to get her to safety when he
comes across Michael Myers.

00:28:41.068 --> 00:28:43.245
He decides to floor it and
try to run Michael over,

00:28:43.245 --> 00:28:44.940
the same tactic that Rachel used

00:28:44.940 --> 00:28:46.140
at the end of "Halloween 4."

00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:47.832
This is where we get the
first big twist of the movie

00:28:47.832 --> 00:28:50.040
where Dr. Sartain attacks
him to prevent him

00:28:50.040 --> 00:28:51.570
from injuring Michael any further.

00:28:51.570 --> 00:28:52.403
We were led to believe

00:28:52.403 --> 00:28:53.972
that Dr. Sartain was the new Dr. Loomis,

00:28:53.972 --> 00:28:56.610
but in fact, he may be the new Dr. Wynn,

00:28:56.610 --> 00:28:58.590
the cult leader from
"Halloween" five and six,

00:28:58.590 --> 00:29:00.360
who essentially acts as Michael's handler.

00:29:00.360 --> 00:29:01.193
Looking back,

00:29:01.193 --> 00:29:03.516
there are a few clues about
Dr. Sartain's true allegiance.

00:29:03.516 --> 00:29:05.580
I already mentioned the
significance of the pen,

00:29:05.580 --> 00:29:06.750
but before the patient transfer,

00:29:06.750 --> 00:29:08.940
Sartain almost seems to be
trying to comfort Michael.

00:29:08.940 --> 00:29:11.790
- Don't worry, Michael.

00:29:11.790 --> 00:29:13.260
I'll be by your side.

00:29:13.260 --> 00:29:14.093
- [Zac] It's already well established

00:29:14.093 --> 00:29:16.901
that Michael's a sociopath, so
there's no reason to do this.

00:29:16.901 --> 00:29:19.110
It's evidence that
Sartain has grown attached

00:29:19.110 --> 00:29:20.776
to his patient. He even
fights to be on the bus,

00:29:20.776 --> 00:29:22.920
most likely a sign that
he had something to do

00:29:22.920 --> 00:29:24.870
with helping The Shape make his escape.

00:29:26.430 --> 00:29:27.930
- Michael Myers is still my patient

00:29:27.930 --> 00:29:30.081
until he's in somebody else's care.

00:29:30.081 --> 00:29:32.580
So, I'm seeing my duty
through until the end.

00:29:32.580 --> 00:29:34.020
- And finally, when Hawkins suggests

00:29:34.020 --> 00:29:35.760
that he's going to kill
Michael if he gets the chance,

00:29:35.760 --> 00:29:37.470
Sartain tries to convince him otherwise,

00:29:37.470 --> 00:29:38.303
even though it's clear

00:29:38.303 --> 00:29:40.620
that they'd be risking the
safety of the townspeople.

00:29:40.620 --> 00:29:42.173
- [Dr. Sartain] Remember,
he's property of the state.

00:29:42.173 --> 00:29:43.631
He mustn't be harmed.

00:29:43.631 --> 00:29:45.780
- Sartain's motive is an interesting case.

00:29:45.780 --> 00:29:46.650
He's a psychologist

00:29:46.650 --> 00:29:48.660
that probably needs his own psychologist.

00:29:48.660 --> 00:29:50.580
He's become so obsessed
with understanding Michael

00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:52.260
that he sees value in putting on the mask

00:29:52.260 --> 00:29:53.884
and seeing what it's like to kill.

00:29:53.884 --> 00:29:56.550
- So, this is what it feels like.

00:29:56.550 --> 00:29:58.470
- [Zac] The fact that he puts
on the mask himself seems

00:29:58.470 --> 00:30:00.330
to pay a tribute to the
original producer's cut

00:30:00.330 --> 00:30:01.980
of "Halloween: The Curse of Michael Myers"

00:30:01.980 --> 00:30:03.885
where Dr. Loomis discovers
Dr. Wynn left behind

00:30:03.885 --> 00:30:05.856
with the iconic mask at
the end of the movie.

00:30:05.856 --> 00:30:08.820
Dr. Sartain's care for his
patient is not mutual however,

00:30:08.820 --> 00:30:10.020
and he gets his head stomped in,

00:30:10.020 --> 00:30:11.430
a fate that he shares with the trash guy

00:30:11.430 --> 00:30:13.110
from Rob Zombie's "Halloween II."

00:30:13.110 --> 00:30:15.450
All of this seems to suggest
that Dr. Sartain is the one

00:30:15.450 --> 00:30:16.800
who sabotaged the patient transfer

00:30:16.800 --> 00:30:18.120
that allowed Michael to get free.

00:30:18.120 --> 00:30:19.590
It's obvious based on his motives

00:30:19.590 --> 00:30:21.120
that he must have had
something to do with it,

00:30:21.120 --> 00:30:21.960
but I find it curious

00:30:21.960 --> 00:30:23.290
that we never actually see the bus crash

00:30:23.290 --> 00:30:24.498
that started all of this.

00:30:24.498 --> 00:30:27.420
My theory is that Laurie
played a hand in it as well.

00:30:27.420 --> 00:30:28.650
We know that she went there with a gun

00:30:28.650 --> 00:30:29.730
to see the patient transfer,

00:30:29.730 --> 00:30:31.920
and it's safe to say that
she's mentally unstable.

00:30:31.920 --> 00:30:32.774
At one point, she even admits

00:30:32.774 --> 00:30:35.130
that she wanted to see Michael escape.

00:30:35.130 --> 00:30:40.130
- Do you know that I pray every
night that he would escape?

00:30:40.500 --> 00:30:41.633
- [Zac] The fact that
this part of the night is

00:30:41.633 --> 00:30:42.841
so deliberately not shown

00:30:42.841 --> 00:30:45.540
in the edit makes me think
Laurie may have cut off the bus

00:30:45.540 --> 00:30:47.850
with her car, causing it to
crash in a roadside ditch.

00:30:47.850 --> 00:30:50.700
Then Dr. Sartain took the
opportunity to use his pen knife

00:30:50.700 --> 00:30:52.620
and fight off the security
guards or the driver.

00:30:52.620 --> 00:30:54.480
As a result, the confrontation
doesn't go the way

00:30:54.480 --> 00:30:55.320
that Laurie had planned,

00:30:55.320 --> 00:30:57.542
and she shows up at Allyson's
dinner emotionally distraught.

00:30:57.542 --> 00:30:59.818
There is a moment where Laurie
sees news about the crash

00:30:59.818 --> 00:31:01.530
on television the next day.

00:31:01.530 --> 00:31:02.520
WCZD.

00:31:02.520 --> 00:31:04.989
Nice. Many people took this as
proof that she didn't do it.

00:31:04.989 --> 00:31:06.572
But if you actually look at this scene,

00:31:06.572 --> 00:31:08.280
she has almost no reaction.

00:31:08.280 --> 00:31:10.380
She doesn't even turn to look at the TV,

00:31:10.380 --> 00:31:12.537
which suggests to me that she
already knew what happened.

00:31:12.537 --> 00:31:14.192
Going back to the scene
where we see her scream,

00:31:14.192 --> 00:31:16.350
who is this figure approaching the car?

00:31:16.350 --> 00:31:17.763
Could this be after she's
already driven the bus

00:31:17.763 --> 00:31:20.580
off the road and now she
doesn't know what to do?

00:31:20.580 --> 00:31:22.487
In my initial video, I did
see a few comments saying

00:31:22.487 --> 00:31:24.418
that test screenings
did actually show Laurie

00:31:24.418 --> 00:31:25.636
as the one who caused the bus crash.

00:31:25.636 --> 00:31:26.775
But since that footage didn't make

00:31:26.775 --> 00:31:27.983
the Blu-Ray deleted scenes,

00:31:27.983 --> 00:31:29.316
maybe that's a twist that they're saving

00:31:29.316 --> 00:31:30.524
for "Halloween Ends."

00:31:30.524 --> 00:31:32.333
Later on, there's a scene
away from the action

00:31:32.333 --> 00:31:34.403
where two cops get into
this weird conversation

00:31:34.403 --> 00:31:36.240
about Bahn Mi Sandwiches.

00:31:36.240 --> 00:31:37.740
The only reason this
conversation seems to be

00:31:37.740 --> 00:31:39.930
in the movie is to make these
cops look kind of goofy.

00:31:39.930 --> 00:31:41.138
I think it's supposed to be a parallel

00:31:41.138 --> 00:31:42.971
to "Halloween 5: The
Revenge of Michael Myers,"

00:31:42.971 --> 00:31:45.330
where these two cop characters
are always accompanied

00:31:45.330 --> 00:31:46.613
by this goofy circus music.

00:31:46.613 --> 00:31:48.330
It's pretty bizarre.

00:31:48.330 --> 00:31:49.620
The cops are killed in the squad car

00:31:49.620 --> 00:31:50.737
while stationed outside of Laurie's house,

00:31:50.737 --> 00:31:52.436
similar to how the
"Halloween 5" cops are killed

00:31:52.436 --> 00:31:54.252
while stationed outside
the teen Halloween party

00:31:54.252 --> 00:31:57.063
at the farm, which is also bizarre.

00:31:58.470 --> 00:31:59.303
I'm gonna throw it over to Jimmy

00:31:59.303 --> 00:32:01.200
who has a few things
you might have missed,

00:32:01.200 --> 00:32:04.080
including who this police
officer character really is.

00:32:04.080 --> 00:32:06.060
- The cop who brings his
own brownies is played

00:32:06.060 --> 00:32:06.893
by Christopher Nelson.

00:32:06.893 --> 00:32:09.096
And he's done makeup
effects work on everything

00:32:09.096 --> 00:32:10.890
from "Avengers: Infinity War,"

00:32:10.890 --> 00:32:12.645
all the way down to these
new "Halloween" movies.

00:32:12.645 --> 00:32:16.050
He also created the masks
you see in "Halloween (2018)"

00:32:16.050 --> 00:32:18.750
and in "Halloween Kills,"
even the flashback mask,

00:32:18.750 --> 00:32:20.490
which I think looks really good.

00:32:20.490 --> 00:32:23.093
The ending of "Halloween (2018)"
was not always the ending

00:32:23.093 --> 00:32:24.570
that we have today.

00:32:24.570 --> 00:32:26.417
This point is about where this version

00:32:26.417 --> 00:32:29.190
and the original version
of the film diverge.

00:32:29.190 --> 00:32:31.080
The outcome in both
versions of the movie is

00:32:31.080 --> 00:32:32.202
pretty much exactly the same,

00:32:32.202 --> 00:32:33.733
but instead of shooting
Michael in the face

00:32:33.733 --> 00:32:35.730
from the top of the basement stairs,

00:32:35.730 --> 00:32:37.507
Karen actually shoots
him on the front porch

00:32:37.507 --> 00:32:38.590
with a crossbow.

00:32:38.590 --> 00:32:40.548
And after he takes a pretty savage beating

00:32:40.548 --> 00:32:41.756
from both her and Laurie,

00:32:41.756 --> 00:32:44.670
he stumbles off into the
woods and sits on a stump.

00:32:44.670 --> 00:32:47.520
Now, I haven't actually
seen the full version

00:32:47.520 --> 00:32:48.660
of the original ending,

00:32:48.660 --> 00:32:50.970
but if you look back to the
trailers for "Halloween (2018),"

00:32:50.970 --> 00:32:52.867
they used a lot of the footage,

00:32:52.867 --> 00:32:55.500
so you can kind of stitch
it together yourself.

00:32:55.500 --> 00:32:56.340
And from what I've heard,

00:32:56.340 --> 00:32:58.800
both Laurie and Michael
are in really rough shape

00:32:58.800 --> 00:32:59.780
in this cut of the movie

00:32:59.780 --> 00:33:01.149
to the point where it's basically implied

00:33:01.149 --> 00:33:02.246
that both of them die.

00:33:02.246 --> 00:33:04.538
But of course, when
Blumhouse and Universal saw

00:33:04.538 --> 00:33:06.510
how good the movie was turning out,

00:33:06.510 --> 00:33:08.220
they decided to alter
the ending a little bit

00:33:08.220 --> 00:33:10.678
to leave it more open
for potential sequels.

00:33:10.678 --> 00:33:12.840
And then it made $250 million.

00:33:12.840 --> 00:33:13.950
The story continues on.

00:33:13.950 --> 00:33:16.080
We get "Halloween Kills"
and "Halloween Ends."

00:33:16.080 --> 00:33:16.968
- Ultimately they did reshoots

00:33:16.968 --> 00:33:18.481
so that the final
confrontation could go down

00:33:18.481 --> 00:33:19.800
inside the house.

00:33:19.800 --> 00:33:21.071
So, to set this up, Laurie
covers the front door

00:33:21.071 --> 00:33:23.160
in order to try to give
her daughter time to hide

00:33:23.160 --> 00:33:25.362
in the basement when this happens.

00:33:25.362 --> 00:33:26.820
(glass breaks)

00:33:26.820 --> 00:33:28.500
The way that Michael reaches
through the front door

00:33:28.500 --> 00:33:30.750
for her is an amped up version
of him smashing his hands

00:33:30.750 --> 00:33:31.710
through the shuttered closet

00:33:31.710 --> 00:33:33.035
and reaching for Laurie in "Halloween."

00:33:33.035 --> 00:33:34.118
After shooting her way free,

00:33:34.118 --> 00:33:35.830
Laurie and Karen take
cover in the basement

00:33:35.830 --> 00:33:38.430
where Laurie has kept
this old gun labeled KS

00:33:38.430 --> 00:33:39.420
for Karen Strode.

00:33:39.420 --> 00:33:41.079
Michael would soon arrive.

00:33:41.079 --> 00:33:42.974
- Hey, Vsauce.

00:33:42.974 --> 00:33:45.307
Michael here.

00:33:45.307 --> 00:33:46.140
- Wrong Michael.

00:33:46.140 --> 00:33:47.250
It's kind of weird

00:33:47.250 --> 00:33:48.556
how they didn't really think
Laurie's house through.

00:33:48.556 --> 00:33:50.389
The basement is located under the kitchen.

00:33:50.389 --> 00:33:52.680
And at one point she shoots
up through the floorboards

00:33:52.680 --> 00:33:53.513
at Michael.

00:33:53.513 --> 00:33:55.170
But when we actually see the
kitchen from the top side,

00:33:55.170 --> 00:33:56.820
it's not floorboards, it's tile.

00:33:56.820 --> 00:33:58.740
As I mentioned before,
the roles are reversed,

00:33:58.740 --> 00:34:00.120
and Laurie is now the hunter.

00:34:00.120 --> 00:34:01.570
This room is identical
to the master bedroom

00:34:01.570 --> 00:34:03.870
where Laurie and Michael fought
at the end of "Halloween,"

00:34:03.870 --> 00:34:05.040
but instead of Michael coming in

00:34:05.040 --> 00:34:07.050
to find the balcony
door open, it's Laurie.

00:34:07.050 --> 00:34:09.232
She follows in Michael's
footsteps by going to the closet,

00:34:09.232 --> 00:34:10.830
but rather than finding Michael,

00:34:10.830 --> 00:34:12.570
she discovers her son-in-law, Ray.

00:34:12.570 --> 00:34:13.585
His corpse is stowed in the same position

00:34:13.585 --> 00:34:16.140
that she found her
friend Lynda in in 1978.

00:34:16.140 --> 00:34:18.240
Michael emerges from
the dark to attack her,

00:34:18.240 --> 00:34:20.276
and she disarms him by jamming
her thumbs into his eyes.

00:34:20.276 --> 00:34:22.770
In the original "Halloween
II," she was able to blind him

00:34:22.770 --> 00:34:24.210
by shooting him directly in the eyes.

00:34:24.210 --> 00:34:26.404
And in the 2007 remake,
Michael blinds Dr. Loomis

00:34:26.404 --> 00:34:28.920
by forcing his thumbs
through his doctor's eyes.

00:34:28.920 --> 00:34:31.680
After Karen's childhood gun
training pays off in a big way,

00:34:31.680 --> 00:34:33.600
Michael is knocked into
the basement by Laurie.

00:34:33.600 --> 00:34:36.000
When he sits up, it's in the
same fashion as his recharge

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:36.833
after being stabbed by Laurie

00:34:36.833 --> 00:34:38.594
in the Doyle's bedroom way back when.

00:34:38.594 --> 00:34:40.697
That's what's crazy
about "Halloween (2018)."

00:34:40.697 --> 00:34:43.050
In their quest to find more
and more classic moments

00:34:43.050 --> 00:34:45.150
to include, they end up
including little mannerisms

00:34:45.150 --> 00:34:46.860
that nobody ever paid much mind to,

00:34:46.860 --> 00:34:48.630
like the way Allyson puts
her hands over her ears

00:34:48.630 --> 00:34:49.742
after hearing a gunshot being a trait

00:34:49.742 --> 00:34:51.350
that she inherited from her grandmother.

00:34:51.350 --> 00:34:52.300
In the beginning of this video,

00:34:52.300 --> 00:34:54.630
I discussed how "Halloween (2018)" is

00:34:54.630 --> 00:34:56.760
kind of a second attempt
at making "Halloween II,"

00:34:56.760 --> 00:34:58.590
and I think the ending solidifies that

00:34:58.590 --> 00:35:00.335
because both movies end
with Laurie playing a part

00:35:00.335 --> 00:35:02.310
in blowing up her evil counterpart,

00:35:02.310 --> 00:35:04.140
and both of these films
could have been the end

00:35:04.140 --> 00:35:06.720
of the franchise with Michael
presumably burning to death,

00:35:06.720 --> 00:35:07.766
but neither of them are.

00:35:07.766 --> 00:35:09.025
I don't know if this was intentional,

00:35:09.025 --> 00:35:11.220
but when Laurie drops the
flare into the basement,

00:35:11.220 --> 00:35:12.448
I couldn't help being
reminded of the sheriff

00:35:12.448 --> 00:35:14.940
dropping the dynamite down
to try to blow Michael up

00:35:14.940 --> 00:35:16.305
at the beginning of "Halloween 5."

00:35:16.305 --> 00:35:18.687
Allyson, Karen, and Laurie
are rescued by a pickup truck,

00:35:18.687 --> 00:35:19.620
which again,

00:35:19.620 --> 00:35:21.660
I couldn't help but think of
our good old Illinois boys

00:35:21.660 --> 00:35:23.790
from "Halloween 4" who
pick up Rachel and Jamie.

00:35:23.790 --> 00:35:25.355
The final shot shows the three generations

00:35:25.355 --> 00:35:27.450
of women huddling in
the back of the truck,

00:35:27.450 --> 00:35:29.400
and Allyson has not let go of the knife.

00:35:29.400 --> 00:35:30.567
My interpretation of this ending is

00:35:30.567 --> 00:35:32.580
that the evening's events
have turned Allyson

00:35:32.580 --> 00:35:33.413
into a fighter.

00:35:33.413 --> 00:35:35.160
All her life, her family has seen Laurie

00:35:35.160 --> 00:35:36.502
as this weird paranoid old woman,

00:35:36.502 --> 00:35:39.201
but now Allyson is going
down that path herself.

00:35:39.201 --> 00:35:41.910
The very, very last thing
we experience is the sound

00:35:41.910 --> 00:35:44.181
of breathing at the end of the credits.

00:35:44.181 --> 00:35:47.098
(masked breathing)

00:35:49.470 --> 00:35:50.541
It's not just breathing though.

00:35:50.541 --> 00:35:52.890
It's the sound of
breathing against a mask,

00:35:52.890 --> 00:35:55.050
which we heard shortly after
Michael first laid eyes

00:35:55.050 --> 00:35:56.400
on Laurie in the original.

00:35:56.400 --> 00:35:58.015
At the time, this was
the only proof we needed

00:35:58.015 --> 00:36:01.020
that "Halloween (2018)"
would have a sequel.

00:36:01.020 --> 00:36:03.420
So, join me for the next
episode of "Things You Missed,"

00:36:03.420 --> 00:36:05.216
where I'll be breaking
down "Halloween Kills."

00:36:05.216 --> 00:36:07.174
And if you wanna hear why you're wrong

00:36:07.174 --> 00:36:08.940
about "Halloween (2018),"

00:36:08.940 --> 00:36:11.295
make sure you check out Jimmy's
"Halloween (2018)" Revisited

00:36:11.295 --> 00:36:12.805
and come on, he's making
some great content.

00:36:12.805 --> 00:36:14.435
Go ahead and just
subscribe to his channel.

00:36:14.435 --> 00:36:16.350
If you're excited for what is in store

00:36:16.350 --> 00:36:17.970
for the finale in "Halloween Ends,"

00:36:17.970 --> 00:36:19.368
make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld

00:36:19.368 --> 00:36:21.229
because I'll absolutely
have an in-depth video

00:36:21.229 --> 00:36:22.530
on that one as well.

00:36:22.530 --> 00:36:24.027
Ring the death bell and
